-/* macOS has no futex_waitv. A wait on one address uses os_sync_wait_on_address (a
- * cross-process futex on shared mappings). A wait on several addresses sleeps on a shared
- * wake generation that wakers bump when someone watches their address. Callers re-check
- * object state after any wake, so a wake meant for someone else only costs a loop. */
-/* Shared wait bookkeeping at the start of the fsync shm (indices below
- * FSYNC_MAC_RESERVED_IDX are never handed out by the server):
- *   base[0]                    wake generation for multi-address waiters
- *   base[4 .. 4+1024)          sleepers on a single address, bucketed by address
- *   base[4+1024 .. 4+2048)     multi-address waiters watching an address, same buckets
